What do we mean by the term “line” in this proof? The length of a line is a constant in Hilbert planes. In a unit square, let $a$ denote the diagonal length. By the Axiom of Congruence, the line of length $a$ meets only the horizontal and vertical lines of the lattice at their points of intersection.

We use the letter $Q$ for a point of intersection between a pair of lines in the diagram because the number of the point $Q$ is defined to be what it is, independent of any application of the Euclidean parallel postulate.

